 PART 1 -- the EXPLICIT H_can (auxiliary scalar sector, DFMP-style)   <-- the missing input
========================================================================================
  Phase space (scalar sector shown; TT gravitons + shift are spectators here):
      (N, pi_N)   lapse pair
      (q, p_q)    conformal pair:  q = -(1/6) ln det gamma,   p_q = -2 gamma_ij pi^ij
  Canonical brackets {N,pi_N}=1, {q,p_q}=1.  Weak-field dictionary (committed convention):
      q     = -Phi/c^2 + O(c^-4)      (q carries the spatial CURVATURE potential Phi ; lensing)
      ln N  = +Psi/c^2 + O(c^-4)      (N carries the LAPSE potential Psi ; slow-matter dynamics)

  EXPLICIT canonical Hamiltonian (MODEL-ASSUMPTION for the kinetic term; DERIVATION for the rest):
      H_can = INT d^3x [  N * C_M^(10)(q, gamma)  +  (sigma/2) p_q^2  +  H_TT  +  H_m  ]
      C_M^(10) = (c^4/4piG) sqrt(g) D_i[ mu_10(y) D^i q ] - sqrt(g) c^2 rho ,   y=(c^2/a0)|Dq|.
  Two facts FORCE the structure (DERIVATION):
    (i)  H_can is LINEAR in N with coefficient C_M  =>  {pi_N,H_can} = -dH_can/dN = -C_M ,
         so preserving the primary S_1=pi_N YIELDS EXACTLY the MOND constraint S_2=C_M^(10).
         This REQUIRES the kernel to ride on q (not ln N): C_M is then N-INDEPENDENT.
    (ii) N-independence of C_M  =>  {pi_N, C_M} = dC_M/dN = 0  (the Embedding-I DICHOTOMY):
         the (pi_N,C_M) pair is NOT itself second-class; second-class-ness is DEFERRED to the
         GENERATED S_3,S_4.  [Contrast Embedding II, kernel on ln N: {pi_N,C_M}=L_N!=0 but then
         dH/dN = C_M + N dC_M/dN != C_M, so pi_N-preservation does NOT give C_M -- fails spec.]
  [PASS] {pi_N,H_can} = -dH_can/dN = -C_M  (pi_N-preservation YIELDS the MOND constraint)
  [PASS] {pi_N,C_M} = dC_M/dN = 0  (Embedding-I dichotomy: C_M is N-independent)
  [info] CHAIN-LENGTH logic (DERIVATION): with H_T=H_can+u*pi_N, the multiplier u first appears in
  [info] dot S_k only when {S_k,pi_N}!=0.  {C_M,pi_N}=0 and {S_3,pi_N}=0 (both N-independent) => the
  [info] chain does NOT stop at S_2 or S_3; it runs to S_4, where {S_4,pi_N}!=0 fixes u and TERMINATES.
  [info] => generically length-4 (the Type-II count), NOT the length-2 'lapse-only' closure of Emb.II.
